    {
      "note": "The italic *for* is the function word the ASV supplies for this appositional numeral phrase, whose own case-function licenses it, so it belongs to the numeral it stands before and is not `added` (rules 33, 7). Head on the numeral, the supplied preposition never being the head (rules 24, 31). This is the chapter's treatment of the same shape in 45:1 (*of five and twenty thousand*), 45:11, 45:14 and 45:23. A competing reading takes the phrase as bare apposition to לַאֲחֻזָּה, whose own *for* is already written, and leaves the second *for* `added`; the phrase has no preposition of its own, so nothing but this noun can carry the word.",
